<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Varman dynasty of Kannauj</h1><p class="st-meta">700 CE – 770 CE (approx.) · capital Kannauj</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The kingdom of Yashovarman, who restored Kannauj's power in the 8th century and patronised the poets Bhavabhuti and Vakpatiraja.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the collapse of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/pushyabhuti-dynasty">Pushyabhuti dynasty</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a> passed through several hands. In the early 8th century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yashovarman-of-kannauj">Yashovarman</a> made it the capital of a powerful kingdom in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges plain</a>. His origins are unknown, and his family is linked by some historians with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/maukharis">Maukharis</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yashovarman-of-kannauj">Yashovarman</a>'s victory over a king of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-magadha">Magadha</a>, probably of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/later-guptas">Later Guptas</a>, is celebrated in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prakrit">Prakrit</a> poem <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaudavaho">Gaudavaho</a> by his court poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vakpatiraja-poet">Vakpatiraja</a>. The great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> dramatist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhavabhuti">Bhavabhuti</a>, author of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttararamacharita">Uttararamacharita</a>, also lived at his court. In 731 he sent an embassy to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a>, possibly seeking allies against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibetans">Tibetans</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yashovarman-of-kannauj">Yashovarman</a> was defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lalitaditya-muktapida">Lalitaditya Muktapida</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/karkota-dynasty">Karkota dynasty</a>, after which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a> was weak. His successors are poorly known, and around 770 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ayudha-dynasty">Ayudha dynasty</a> took Kannauj.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/varman-dynasty-of-kannauj.jpg" alt="Varman dynasty of Kannauj" width="320" height="147"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coinage_of_Yasovarman.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>700 CE – 770 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kannauj</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Yashovarman</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sanskrit, Prakrit</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Yashovarman</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=735&amp;focus=varman-dynasty-of-kannauj" aria-label="Varman dynasty of Kannauj on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6783 1186 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Varman dynasty of Kannauj lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7103 1442L6905 1198M7103 1442L7103 1442"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6905 1198h0M7103 1442h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7103 1442h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7103 1442h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kannauj. <a href="/atlas?year=735&amp;focus=varman-dynasty-of-kannauj">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
